# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Propene (propylene) CH2=CH-CH3: C=C 1.336 A, C-C 1.501 A, C=C-C 124.3 degrees, C-H 1.085 A (vinyl) / 1.094 A (methyl).
# Geometry: NIST CCCBDB experimental, rounded (Angstrom converted at 1 A = 1.8897261 Bohr); the experimental geometry, not this
# solver's minimum (LSDA on a grid relaxes it slightly: press Relax to see where).
# A 16 Bohr box at h = 0.15 (the app's default grid) under the default ionic potential.
grid 107 0.15
charge 0
ionic accepted
